# Sardeenz v2 — local development configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and adjust to avoid port clashes with other projects:
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#
# This single file drives every local service and the compose stack:
#   - compose.yaml reads it automatically (host-port mappings + Postgres credentials)
#   - the Rust proxy loads it via dotenvy; the Node services (control plane, dashboard
#     BFF, dev worker) load it via loadRootEnv(); Vite loads it via loadEnv()
#
# Values already set in the real environment always win over this file, so per-process
# overrides (e.g. `SARDEENZ_WORKER_PORT=9200 make dev-worker`) still work. Every value
# below is the built-in default — uncomment and change only what you need.

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Container host-port mappings (compose.yaml)
# Only the HOST side changes; the in-container ports stay fixed. If you change one
# of these, update the matching connection URL further down so the apps still connect.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_REDIS_HOST_PORT=6379
# SARDEENZ_POSTGRES_HOST_PORT=5432

# Postgres credentials (compose.yaml + SARDEENZ_DATABASE_URL below must agree)
# SARDEENZ_POSTGRES_USER=sardeenz
# SARDEENZ_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=sardeenz
# SARDEENZ_POSTGRES_DB=sardeenz

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Shared connection URLs (consumed by the apps)
# Keep the ports here in sync with the host-port mappings above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379
# SARDEENZ_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://sardeenz:sardeenz@localhost:5432/sardeenz

# Integration tests run against a DEDICATED database (derived by suffixing the DB name with
# `_test`, e.g. sardeenz_test, auto-created on first run) and Redis logical DB 1 — never your dev
# data. Override only if you need a different test target; the harness refuses any DB not ending
# in `_test` unless SARDEENZ_ALLOW_NON_TEST_DB=1. See docs/development/setup.md.
# SARDEENZ_TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://sardeenz:sardeenz@localhost:5432/sardeenz_test
# SARDEENZ_TEST_REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379/1

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Routing proxy (Rust)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_PROXY_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:8080   # OpenAI-compatible inference endpoint
# SARDEENZ_ADMIN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:9099          # health + metrics

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Control plane (TypeScript)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_CONTROL_PLANE_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:3000   # bind address
# SARDEENZ_CONTROL_PLANE_URL=http://localhost:3000  # how the proxy + BFF reach it

# Single-instance mode — required when running outside Kubernetes.
# The control plane will self-elect as leader without a Kubernetes Lease.
# SARDEENZ_SINGLE_INSTANCE=true

# Shared-secret API auth. When set, the control plane requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>` on
# every /api/v1/* request; the proxy (wake triggers) and dashboard BFF read the same value and send
# it automatically. Leave unset for local dev — authentication is disabled and a startup warning is
# logged. Set this in any deployment reachable outside a trusted network (see
# docs/usage/deployment-security.md).
# SARDEENZ_API_TOKEN=

# Shared-secret worker agent auth. When set, each worker requires `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
# on every /runners* request (except /healthz); the control plane's WorkerClient reads the same
# value and sends it automatically. Set the identical value on the worker and the control plane.
# Leave unset for local dev — authentication is disabled and a startup warning is logged. Set this
# in any deployment reachable outside a trusted network (see docs/usage/deployment-security.md).
# SARDEENZ_WORKER_TOKEN=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard BFF (TypeScript)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_BFF_LISTEN_ADDR=0.0.0.0:4000
# SARDEENZ_PROMETHEUS_URL=http://localhost:9090
# SARDEENZ_SERVE_STATIC=1                            # serve built SPA from dist/client outside production (e2e/preview); prod serves it automatically
# SARDEENZ_CLIENT_DIR=/abs/path/to/dashboard/dist/client  # overrides the static-client directory (used by e2e); leave unset in production so it resolves the compiled dist/client

# Public origin the BFF is reached at (e.g. https://sardeenz.example.com). Required when
# AUTH_MODE=oauth (used to build the OAuth redirect_uri) and used to decide whether the SSE auth
# cookie gets Secure set, since the BFF sits behind a reverse proxy/ingress and can't infer its
# own external scheme/host from the request. Leave unset for local dev. See
# docs/usage/deployment-security.md.
# SARDEENZ_PUBLIC_URL=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dashboard dev server (Vite)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_DASHBOARD_PORT=5173
# SARDEENZ_BFF_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:4000   # /api proxy target; match SARDEENZ_BFF_LISTEN_ADDR

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dev workers (a second worker via `make dev-worker-2` uses +100 offsets)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SARDEENZ_WORKER_PORT=9100
# SARDEENZ_RUNNER_PORT_START=9101
# SARDEENZ_WORKER_ADVERTISE_HOST=localhost        # advertised address; in-cluster set from status.podIP

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Runner catalog (control plane loads this and shows it on the dashboard)
# Accepts an http(s) URL, a local file path, or a file:// URL.
# The built-in default is the remote official catalog, which requires network access
# — for local dev, point at the in-repo runners.yaml instead. Uncomment ONE:
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Local (dev): path is relative to the control-plane process cwd (control-plane/),
# so ../runners.yaml is the repo-root file. Use an absolute path if you launch it elsewhere.
# SARDEENZ_RUNNER_CATALOG_URL=../runners.yaml
# Remote (default): the official published catalog (needs internet).
# SARDEENZ_RUNNER_CATALOG_URL=https://raw.githubusercontent.com/rh-aiservices-bu/school-of-sardeenz/refs/heads/main/runners.yaml

# SIF signature verification (`apptainer verify`), enforced at catalog import (control plane) AND
# at exec (worker). Default true. Set to false ONLY for experimentation with unsigned SIFs, when you
# have no CI/librarian signing key yet — then build+push with plain `apptainer build`/`apptainer push`
# (skip `apptainer sign`; do not use scripts/build-sif.sh, which refuses unsigned).
# SECURITY: unsigned means anything with write access to the module store/registry can run code on
# your GPUs. Keep such an instance inside a trusted sandbox and RE-ENABLE this (with a shared signing
# key) before exposing or sharing the deployment. See docs/usage/runner-catalog.md.
# SARDEENZ_VERIFY_SIF=false

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Worker apptainer mode — run real engine SIFs locally instead of the in-process stub.
# REQUIRES: `apptainer` on PATH, a GPU (the launcher adds --nv for CUDA runners), and a model
# staged under SARDEENZ_WEIGHTS_DIR. Without a GPU, leave the worker in the default 'stub' mode.
# The worker execs ${SARDEENZ_MODULES_DIR}/<runtimeModule>.sif (e.g. .../vllm-0.21.sif); drop your
# SIF there, named to match the sifName/id you deploy. The control plane scans the same dir and
# lists it. For unsigned local SIFs, also set SARDEENZ_VERIFY_SIF=false above.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Use ABSOLUTE paths (control plane and worker run from different cwds). The apptainer bind mounts
# and HOME derive from the weights/scratch dirs below, so for local dev you normally only set these:
# SARDEENZ_WORKER_MODE=apptainer                     # default 'stub' (fake runner, no SIF touched)
# SARDEENZ_MODULES_DIR=/home/you/sardeenz/modules    # where <runtimeModule>.sif files live (default /modules)
# SARDEENZ_WEIGHTS_DIR=/home/you/sardeenz/weights    # model weights (default /weights). Bind-mounted into the SIF;
#                                                    # also browsed by the control plane for the dashboard model-path picker
#                                                    # (the control plane must be able to read this dir).
# SARDEENZ_SCRATCH_DIR=/home/you/sardeenz/scratch    # scratch/caches; HOME defaults to <scratch>/home (default /scratch)
# SARDEENZ_APPTAINER_BIN=apptainer                   # override if apptainer isn't on PATH
# Advanced overrides (default to the dirs above — rarely needed):
# SARDEENZ_APPTAINER_BINDS=/home/you/sardeenz/weights,/home/you/sardeenz/scratch  # default: WEIGHTS_DIR,SCRATCH_DIR
# SARDEENZ_APPTAINER_HOME=/home/you/sardeenz/scratch/home                         # default: <SCRATCH_DIR>/home
